@startuml
!include style.puml
actor "CLI User" as Visitor
actor "Authenticated Developer" as Developer
rectangle IranAPI {
  usecase "UC-15\nUse IranAPI CLI" as Main
  usecase "Doctor / catalog / docs / schema" as Public
  usecase "Call public URL" as Call
  usecase "Store or remove token" as Token
  usecase "Who am I / raw request" as Private
  usecase "Analyze or deploy project" as Project
  usecase "Resolve runtime API base URL" as BaseUrl
}
Visitor --> Public
Visitor --> Call
Developer --> Token
Developer --> Private
Developer --> Project
Public ..> Main : <<extend>>
Call ..> Main : <<extend>>
Token ..> Main : <<extend>>
Private ..> Main : <<extend>>
Project ..> Main : <<extend>>
Main ..> BaseUrl : <<include>>
note bottom of Token
login validates and stores an existing token;
it does not accept username/password.
end note
note bottom of BaseUrl
Temporary domains can be selected with --api-url,
IRANAPI_API_URL, or saved configuration.
end note
@enduml
